course: dictionary
lesson: 6809
title: Finding where a word comes from
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Origin means where or how something began. «The origin of the river is a small spring high in the hills» tells you the river starts there. Look for clue words like «origin of» and ask yourself: where or how did this start?
explain: A person's origins are the country, family or background they come from. «Maya's family has origins in Pakistan» tells you where her family is from. In maths, the origin is the point (0, 0) where the x-axis and y-axis meet on a graph.
explain: Words have origins too. «The exact origin is not known» means nobody is sure where a phrase like «Break a leg» first came from. Some words from Greek use «rh», «ph» and «y», and words from French often end in «-ette» or «-ue», which can help you guess.
fact: Origin means where or how something began.
fact: A person's origins are the country, family or background they come from.
fact: In maths, the origin is the point (0, 0) where the x-axis and y-axis meet.
fact: «Country of origin» on a food label tells you which country the food comes from.
fact: Words from Greek often use «rh», «ph» and «y», as in «rhythm».
exercise: «The origin of the river is a small spring high in the hills.» What does origin mean here? | The name of its fish | *Where it begins | The deepest part of the water | Where it ends in the sea
exercise: «The exact origin is not known.» What does origin mean in this sentence? | The meaning of the word | *Where or how it began | The date it was printed | The person who wrote it
exercise: On a graph, the origin is where the x-axis and y-axis meet. What is its position? | (5, 5) | (10, 0) | (1, 1) | *(0, 0)
test: Maya's family has origins in Pakistan. What does origins mean here? | The school she goes to | The games she plays at break | *The country, family or background her family comes from | The food she likes best
test: Words from Greek often use «rh», «ph» and «y». What does this tell you? | The word has no origin at all | *The word's origin may be Greek | The word is a number | The word is probably about the sea
exam: Which sentence uses origin to mean a person's background? | *Her origins are in Brazil, where her grandparents were born. | Plot the points from the origin first. | The origin of the bus is the bus stop. | The origin of the graph is at (0, 0).
